+## Before-session failure
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, both `processMessage` and `processMessageStream` await `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model processing begins ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
+`afterSession` runs even if initialization never completed: it guarantees a cleanup opportunity, not a successfully started session. A deployer must track its own allocations (including partial allocations before a throw) and release only resources it actually acquired; the hook receives the same session and no additional initialization-status argument.
+
